# Canonical host.
#
# www.ai.wolfpackmediapr.com exists only to catch people who type "www." out of
# habit. Netlify serves a domain alias as-is, so without this rule the same app
# answers on two hostnames -- which splits SEO, makes support ambiguous, and
# means auth redirects could come back to a host the session was not set on.
# Force it to the canonical address instead. The "!" is required because the SPA
# rule below would otherwise match first.
https://www.ai.wolfpackmediapr.com/*  https://ai.wolfpackmediapr.com/:splat  301!

# SPA fallback: every other path is handled by the client-side router.
/*    /index.html   200
